\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Copies the directory or file specified in path 
\i source
\i0  to a different location in the file system identified by pathname 
\i destination
\i0 . If 
\i source
\i0  is a file, the method creates a file at 
\i destination
\i0  that holds the exact contents of the original file (this includes UNIX special files). If 
\i source
\i0  is a directory, the method creates a new directory at 
\i destination
\i0  and recursively populates it with duplicates of the files and directories contained in 
\i source
\i0 , preserving all links. The file specified in 
\i source
\i0  must exist, while 
\i destination
\i0  must not exist prior to the operation. When a file is being copied, the 
\i destination
\i0  path must end in a file name; there is no implicit adoption of the 
\i source
\i0  file name. Symbolic links are not traversed but are themselves copied.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 If the copy operation is successful, the method returns YES. If the operation is not successful, but the callback 
\i handler
\i0  of 
\b fileManager:shouldProceedAfterError:
\b0  returns YES (see below), 
\b copyPath:toPath:handler:
\b0  also returns YES. Otherwise this copy method returns NO. The method also attempts to make the attributes of the directory or file at 
\i destination
\i0  identical to 
\i source
\i0 , but ignores any failure at this attempt.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 The argument 
\i handler
\i0  identifies an object that responds to the callback messages 
\b fileManager:willProcessPath:
\b0  or  
\b fileManager:shouldProceedAfterError:
\b0 . This callback mechanism is similar to delegation. NSFileManager sends the first message when it begins a copy, move, remove, or link operation. It sends the second message when it encounters any error in processing. You can specify 
\b nil
\b0  for 
\i handler
\i0  if no object responds to the callback messages. (See the descriptions of 
\b fileManager:willProcessPath:
\b0  or  
\b fileManager:shouldProceedAfterError:
\b0  at the end of this specification for details on these methods.)\

\fs14 \

\fs28 This code fragment verifies that the file to be copied exists and then copies that file to the user's 
\b ~/Library/Reports
\b0  directory:\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx2400\tx2880\tx3420\tx3940\tx4440\tx4920\tx7000\tx7500\tx8000\tx8500\tx9020\tx9520\tx10020\tx10520\tx11020\tx11500\f4\fs24\li1900\fc0\cf0 NSString *source = @"/tmp/quarterly_report.rtf";\
NSString *destination = [[NSHomeDirectory()\
	stringByAppendingPathComponent:@"Library"]\
	stringByAppendingPathComponent:@"Reports"];\
NSFileManager *manager = [NSFileManager defaultManager];\
if ([manager fileExistsAtPath:source])\
      [manager copyPath:source toPath:destination handler:nil];\
\

\fs14 \

