\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Returns the path of the program's current directory. Relative pathnames refer implictly to this directory; for example, if the current directory is
\b  /tmp
\b0 , and the relative pathname is 
\b reports/info.txt
\b0 , the full pathname is constructed as 
\b /tmp/reports/info.txt
\b0 . This path is initialized to the current working directory, and can be thereafter reset with 
\b changeCurrentDirectoryPath:
\b0 . If the application's current working directory isn't accessible, this method returns 
\b nil
