\b0  creates a new directory at 
\i destination
\i0  and recursively populates it with duplicates of the files and directories contained in 
\i source
\i0 ; it then deletes the old directory and its contents. The file specified in 
\i source
\i0  must exist, while 
\i destination
\i0  must not yet exist. The 
\i destination
\i0  path must end in a file name; there is no implicit adoption of the 
